{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1331326-biting-the-geryo-for-essence-and-aggravated-damage","id":1331326,"title":"Biting the Geryo for Essence and Aggravated damage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-17T05:19:56-07:00","id":1331326,"title":"Biting the Geryo for Essence and Aggravated damage","content":"I am a little fuzzy on Aggravated damage that Uratha can cause with a bite for Essence, does it only apply to other Uratha or does it also apply to other things like Geryo or Idigam which have essence as well? It says Wolf and man so is that also regular humans and therefore things like vampires and Mages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T06:23:52-07:00","id":1331329,"title":"","content":"I would say that it could work.. but as they are Natural Carriers for the Geryo Strain, you would be essentially infecting yourself with the Contagion.. so I definitely would absolutely advise against it under every possible circumstance imaginable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T09:39:39-07:00","id":1331344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1331326-biting-the-geryo-for-essence-and-aggravated-damage?p=1331329#post1331329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that it could work.. but as they are Natural Carriers for the Geryo Strain, you would be essentially infecting yourself with the Contagion.. so I definitely would absolutely advise against it under every possible circumstance imaginable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point! I never thought of that. I just figured that Aggravated damage might be the only way to even have a chance of defeating one since some of them seem extremely powerful with healing rates that would make lethal damage too ineffective to stop them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T13:20:06-07:00","id":1331376,"title":"","content":"I'd let Urfarah's Bane work on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T17:12:05-07:00","id":1331404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1331326-biting-the-geryo-for-essence-and-aggravated-damage#post1331326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a little fuzzy on Aggravated damage that Uratha can cause with a bite for Essence, does it only apply to other Uratha or does it also apply to other things like Geryo or Idigam which have essence as well? It says Wolf and man so is that also regular humans and therefore things like vampires and Mages?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just having an Essence trait is not enough or werewolves would be able to devour spirits for Essence without the Siskur-Dah. No, they gain it from consuming the flesh of wolves and humans (and werewolves) just like a spirit of a consuming fire would gain Essence from consuming fire and hunger spirits. Draining Essence already stored as Essence requires other ways (such as the Siskur-Dah or by binding the Essence in a Fetish first).<br /> So it does not work on idigam or the First Geryo, might work on Distorted werewolves, and most likely not work on vampires as they're spiritually not human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T18:46:24-07:00","id":1331425,"title":"","content":"As the last true half-Primordials, I\u2019d allow Urfarah\u2019s Bane to work on Geryo. (Most Uratha who take on a Geryo who isn\u2019t already fixated on a different prey is probably going to find themselves subject to the Geryo\u2019s sacred hunt and suffer the same bane in return.) I\u2019d also allow Uratha to inflict Aggravated by consuming Geryo flesh, but would count such as directly contracting the Geryo strain and moving straight onto progress of the disease with a negative modifier equal to how much flesh she consumed (-1 per box of aggravated damage inflicted). <br /> <br /> Uratha can consume flesh for aggravated from Distorted (they\u2019re still werewolves), with the same risks if the Distorted has the infectious mutation.<br /> <br /> This is a case where the natural tools available to the Uratha carry considerable risk and they need to seriously consider whether they want to go down that path. I\u2019d also suggest having some NPC Uratha try is first and succumb to the agonzing warping disease before surprise springing it on your players, so they know it\u2019s a risk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}